menu "NOVA"

config NOVA_BACKEND_URL
    string "Backend base URL"
    default "wss://localhost:8000"
    help
        Base URL of the NOVA backend, without a path. The device appends
        /api/v1/devices/ws.

        Compiled in rather than provisioned at runtime: pointing a device at a
        different backend should be a firmware change. A runtime-settable
        server URL is a way to redirect somebody's device to an attacker.

        Use wss://, not ws://. The device token travels in the query string,
        and over ws:// it travels in clear text to anything on the path.

config NOVA_FIRMWARE_VERSION
    string "Firmware version"
    default "0.1.0"
    help
        Reported in every heartbeat. The dashboard uses it to tell which
        devices are running which build, which is the difference between "one
        user has a problem" and "the last release has a problem".

endmenu
